  "question": {
    "text": "A plano-convex lens has a radius of curvature of the curved surface equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and a refractive index equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>,&nbsp; then what is the focal length (in <math> <mrow> <mtext>cm</mtext></mrow> </math>) of the lens?"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "60.00",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>∝</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>cm</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mo>∞</mo></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>30</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mi>cm</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace></math></p>"
